While playing nethack there suddenly was a memory fault :-(
The situation: nethack 3.0 with patches 1, 2 and 3 on a Unix V.2 system,
character Valkerie, level 19, in a dark room, with no monster nearby.
Str 18/07, Hp 92(99) Ac -5, speed boots, gauntlets of power, +4 long sword.
I walked through the room (might be I grabbed something from the floor) 
and then the game suddenly stopped with the message: "Memory fault"
and no dump (special save file or a Unix 'core' file) was made. No need
to tell that the terminal was also not restored to its default setting.
I have no idea what happend. It is the first time I was this deep in the
dungeon, and no one else around here has been this far, so I do not know
whether this is a one time shot or happens all the time.
On our machine we have a restriction of 1.5M process space. Might this
cause problems when having found lots of stuff ?
When being in wizzard mode I could go to level 26 without problems, using
only something like 700K.

One of the patch level 3 patches did not work. Probably the 'pickup' which
was send as an extra patch just after patch level 2. Patch said something
like: "Hmmm, this looks like an already installed patch. Do you want to reverse
this patch ?" and then I typed: "NO". I hope this is correct.

While being on the net I have just one more question: it seems as if level
(say about) 7 until 19 (or deeper if you can get there :-) are *very*
uninterresting. I almost didn't encounter any terrible monster. At most one
monster per level (besides some minor monsters like Orcs/Bats etc).
I expected these levels to be *much* harder. Is this normal or am I already
too strong ?
In nethack 2.3 the levels did increase in difficulty. Now it seems as if
once you made it through the first 8, you have no problem until level 20.

And of course another general remark: shouldn't you be able to move
heavy chests (which you cannot lift anymore) like you move large boulders
and push them off the stairs to a lower level? Seems quite natural doesn't it?
